---
title: Alternating Incline Dumbbell Press (30°)
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9b1a612-ed57-4144-bde1-1a7dfd8393be)


{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Set the bench to a 30-degree incline.

### Step 2
Grab the dumbbells and lie back on the bench, holding both weights straight up above your chest with your palms facing forward.

### Step 3
Keep a slight natural arch in your lower back, pull your shoulders down away from your ears, and squeeze your shoulder blades firmly against the bench. Plant your feet wide and flat on the floor for stability.

### Step 4
Inhale and slowly lower one dumbbell down to chest level while keeping the other arm extended straight up.

### Step 5
Squeeze your chest muscles and exhale as you press the dumbbell back up to the top. Repeat the movement on the other side.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• To protect your shoulder joints, keep your elbows angled slightly below 90 degrees relative to your torso (around 60–75 degrees) and move them down in a straight vertical line.

• Keep your shoulder blades pressed firmly against the bench throughout the entire set.

• Avoid over-arching your lower back and do not aggressively lock out your elbows at the top.
{{< /callout >}}
